WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.075
Who does the work?

2
00:00:01.075 --> 00:00:06.605
The master plan estimated the program
office and workstreams at about five and a

3
00:00:06.605 --> 00:00:11.970
half full-time equivalents, for an
illustrative 52-week program: half a steward;

4
00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:16.427
a full-time infrastructure lead,
identity lead and endpoint lead;

5
00:00:16.427 --> 00:00:20.637
and half-time DNS, PKI and security
leads and a project manager.

6
00:00:20.637 --> 00:00:23.349
It's a planning model,
not a staffing standard.

7
00:00:23.349 --> 00:00:26.463
What matters more is what
the estimate leaves out:

8
00:00:26.463 --> 00:00:29.880
application owners for every
application that moves,

9
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:34.056
help desk capacity for every wave,
HR and contractor-source owners,

10
00:00:34.056 --> 00:00:37.321
records and privacy, and
the CISO's and authorizing

11
00:00:37.321 --> 00:00:40.662
official's time for requirements
and risk decisions.

12
00:00:40.662 --> 00:00:44.725
The program can't run without them,
so budget for them explicitly.

13
00:00:44.725 --> 00:00:47.050
And cross-train two people per workstream.

14
00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:48.956
The rhythm: daily standups,

15
00:00:48.956 --> 00:00:53.462
and a weekly report rating each
workstream green, yellow or red.

16
00:00:53.462 --> 00:00:56.350
The steering committee
meets every two weeks,

17
00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:59.847
the steward and sponsor review
gate readiness monthly,

18
00:00:59.847 --> 00:01:04.787
and each gate gets a ninety-minute review
that ends in go, no-go or conditional go.

19
00:01:04.787 --> 00:01:08.774
And two consecutive red weeks for
any workstream go to the sponsor.

20
00:01:08.774 --> 00:01:14.104
The decision for the sponsor and CIO: put
those people in the Phase 0 business case,

21
00:01:14.104 --> 00:01:18.700
alongside the licenses, and approve
the budget before design begins.
